-connections/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">6ac8231c0032f6bb7ef3fffa</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:30:00 +0000</pubDate><ns1:content /><description>Here’s what we know about the record-setting El Niño on a record-hot planet, and the most important questions scientists are trying to answer.</description><category>Science</category><category>Science / Environment</category><ns1:keywords>El Nino, extreme weather, climate, climate change</ns1:keywords><dc:publisher>Condé Nast</dc:publisher><dc:subject>Hot Stuff</dc:subject><ns1:thumbnail url="https://media.wired.com/photos/6ac8231cca19e55033ce8ba8/master/pass/cambio%20clim%C3%A1tico%20El%20Ni%C3%B1o%202298072299.jpg" width="3000" height="1688" /></item></channel></rss>